        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Visionaries: Leonardo, Darwin, Faraday, Tesla",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "These are not scientists who did good science.\n  They are scientists who saw *categories that didn't yet exist*\n  and spent their careers trying to fill them."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md#004",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries, git-history:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries]",
        "canonical_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "current_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:visionaries:scientific-visionaries",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "visionaries",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Visionaries: Leonardo, Darwin, Faraday, Tesla",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Leonardo da Vinci (1452–1519):\n  Saw mechanisms before the materials existed to build them.\n  Tank, helicopter, solar concentrator, ball bearing,\n  parachute, hang glider — all 500 years before deployment.\n  His failure: no mathematical formalism; brilliant drawings,\n  no transmission mechanism."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md#005",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries, git-history:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries]",
        "canonical_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "current_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:visionaries:scientific-visionaries",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "visionaries",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Visionaries: Leonardo, Darwin, Faraday, Tesla",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Charles Darwin (1809–1882):\n  Saw that life's diversity has a single mechanical explanation:\n  variation + selection + time.\n  \"Nothing in biology makes sense except in the light of\n  evolution.\" (Dobzhansky, 1973 — but Darwin's insight, 1859)\n  His vision: universal descent with modification.\n  Not just a theory of biology — a theory of how complexity\n  can arise without a designer."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md#006",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries, git-history:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries]",
        "canonical_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "current_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:visionaries:scientific-visionaries",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "visionaries",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Visionaries: Leonardo, Darwin, Faraday, Tesla",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Michael Faraday (1791–1867):\n  Saw that electricity and magnetism were manifestations of\n  the same underlying phenomenon — field theory.\n  Maxwell turned his intuition into equations.\n  Every electric motor, generator, transformer = Faraday's vision."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md#007",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries, git-history:visionaries:03-scientific-visionaries]",
        "canonical_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "current_path": "visionaries/03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:visionaries:scientific-visionaries",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "visionaries",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, visionaries]",
        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Visionaries: Leonardo, Darwin, Faraday, Tesla",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Nikola Tesla (1856–1943):\n  Saw the practical electrical system — AC not DC, rotating\n  magnetic fields, wireless transmission — before it was built.\n  Most of it was built. Defeated Edison's DC system.\n  Died broke and misunderstood; the predictions that came true\n  were already proven; the predictions still pending (Wardenclyffe\n  = wireless global power transmission) may still come true."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-VISIONARIES.md#008",
      "path": [
